 "text": "Martin County\nCommunity\nCities\nCommunity Links\nCounty History\nCourthouse History\nParks\nFacilities\nMap\nRules\nBright Lake\nCedar Hanson\nKlessig\nPerch Lake\nTimberlane\nWolter\nSchools\nYour Government\nAdvertisement for Bids\nBoard of Commissioners\nAgendas/Minutes\nDistrict 1\nDistrict 2\nDistrict 3\nDistrict 4\nDistrict 5\nData Practices\nDepartments\nAssessor\nAuditor/Treasurer\nCoordinator\nCounty Attorney\nDrainage Administration\nEconomic Development\nExtension\nHighway\nHuman Resources\nHuman Services\nInformation Technology\nLibrary\nPlanning & Zoning\nProbation\nPublic Transit\nRecorder\nRecycling/Solid Waste\nSheriff\nVeteran Services\nVictim/Witness\nDistrict Court\nLaw Library\nElections\nElection Judges\nPublic Officials Guide\nFee Schedule\nObserved Holidays\nOrdinances\nSalary Compliance\nI Want To\nApply\nProperty Tax Abatement\nFind\nActive Warrants\nJail Roster\nProperty Information\nSafe At Home Info\nPay\nFines\nProperty Taxes\nVote\nContact Us\nTranslate\nSelect your language.\nEnglish\nSpanish\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nmore Languages\nEnglish\nAfrikaans\nAlbanian\nArabic\nArmenian\nAzerbaijani\nBasque\nBelarusian\nBengali\nBosnian\nBulgarian\nCatalan\nCebuano\nChinese (Simplified)\nChinese (Traditional)\nCroatian\nCzech\nDanish\nDutch\nEsperanto\nEstonian\nFilipino\nFinnish\nFrench\nGalician\nGeorgian\nGerman\nGreek\nGujarati\nHaitian Creole\nHausa\nHebrew\nHindi\nHmong\nHungarian\nIcelandic\nIgbo\nIndonesian\nIrish\nItalian\nJapanese\nJavanese\nKannada\nKhmer\nKorean\nLao\nLatin\nLatvian\nLithuanian\nMacedonian\nMalay\nMaltese\nMaori\nMarathi\nMongolian\nNepali\nNorwegian\nPersian\nPolish\nPortuguese\nPunjabi\nRomanian\nRussian\nSerbian\nSlovak\nSlovenian\nSomali\nSpanish\nSwahili\nSwedish\nTamil\nTelugu\nThai\nTurkish\nUkrainian\nUrdu\nVietnamese\nWelsh\nYiddish\nYoruba\nZulu\nServices!\nForms!\nAll Of Martin!\nServices!\nForms!\nAll Of Martin!\nslide 1 of 1\nAssessor\nHome\nYour Government\nDepartments\nAssessor\nSub Menu\nPage Menu\nAssessor's Home\nApplications & Forms\nBeacon Property Search\nProperty Tax Homestead Notice\nServices & Fees\nThe State of Minnesota is experiencing estimated market value increases on most property types including agricultural land, residential / seasonal, commercial / industrial and recreational land. It is important to remember that increasing property values does not mean the taxing jurisdictions (cities, school districts, townships, counties) are collecting more revenue. The estimated market value is used to determine a parcel's share of the total tax bill that needs to be collected based on the budgeting of those jurisdictions.\nIn other words, if the 2025 budgets of cities, townships, and the county stay the same or minimally increase for 2025 then taxes paid by property owners will not rise at the same rate as the value. Property taxes are decided based on the budget that needs to be met.\nWhere can I learn about property taxes? Check out the MN Department of Revenue property tax website. Or, here is a helpful video from Ramsey County explaining property tax basics, and another from Anoka County titled Pie, With a Side of Property Taxes .\nWithin these pages you can discover how property is valued and classified , what role Estimated Market Value has in your property taxes, and how to appeal your property value and classification .\nDiscover resources for Homestead , Veterans with a Disability , and Special Homestead for Property Owners who are Blind or Disabled , Property Tax Refund and Senior Property Tax Deferral .\nContact your County Assessor for more information or explanations. We are here to help.\nSALES DATA\nGenerate sales lists using multiple criteria.\nOr from a Beacon Parcel Report, scroll to bottom and use Recent Sales in Area by Neighborhood or Distance.\nReview Sales Ratio Reports to verify Assessor compliance.\n*PROPERTY TAX HOMESTEAD NOTICE*\nCredits and Exclusions:\nMore information about Classification Rates , Local Tax Rates , Homestead Exclusion Calculation , Special Ag Qualification Flow Charts , Ag Credit , School Building Bond Credit , Powerline Credit .\nAbatements:\nConsidering building new housing? Check out the Housing Property Tax Abatement\nInquire with the EDA about Business Subsidy Agreements\nDisaster Relief Get Application\nWhat is: PILT - Payment In Lieu of Taxes?\nThe Assessor's Role:\nThe primary job of the assessor's office is actually narrower than most taxpayers believe. Their task is to value and classify each property in the county. An assessor doesn't decide how much tax is to be paid nor do they establish tax rates. Estimated Market Value is the assessor's estimate of a property's actual market value, defined as the most probable price well informed buyers and sellers would agree to without either party being unduly forced to buy or sell on the assessment date, January 2, each year.\nThe assessor's office maintains property information to assist in annual valuation estimates. This data is available on Beacon . Appraisers review the information for each property in the county at least once every 5 years to ensure accuracy. This allows comparing all unsold properties to properties that have sold recently to help estimate market value.\nMain Office Number 507-238-3210\nCounty Assessor\nJessica Laue\n507-238-3278\njessica.laue@martincountymn.gov\n|\n|\nCounty Appraisers |\n|\nJeremiah Fitzgerald\n507-238-3108\njeremiah.fitzgerald@martincountymn.gov\n|\n|\nTanner Menke\n507-238-3251\ntanner.menke@martincountymn.gov |\n|\nNick Sandberg\n507-238-3109\nnick.sandberg@martincountymn.gov |\n|\nTerri Schrader\n507-238-3253\nterri.schrader@martincountymn.gov |\n|\nCrystal Utesch\n507-238-3250\ncrystal.utesch@martincountymn.gov\n|\n|\nServices and Fees |\nCopies |\n$.25 |\nField Sheet Reports or Copies |\n$1.00 |\nPre-programmed Computer Reports |\n$5.00 plus $.10 per page |\nData Download Reports |\n$60 setup fee + $.06 per parcel |\nCD Production |\n$5.00 |\nFaxing Fee |\n$5.00 |\nChecks may be made to Martin County |\nShare this page\nShare this page\n-->\nClose\nContact Us!\n201 Lake Avenue Fairmont, MN 56031\n507-238-3124\nOpen 8:00 am - 5:00 pm, M - F\nContact Us\nQuicklinks!\nAgendas & Minutes\nDocument Center\nJail Roster\nEmployment Opportunities\nPublic Notices\nProperty Search\nPublic Officials Guide\nCommissioner Login\nCounty Email\nEmployee Login\nPowered by revize., the Government Website Experts | Login\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate\nClose Read More",
